+## 0.2.0: source provenance and assessment protocol 1
+
+Source evidence_level is independent of judgment. Supported AI/human assessments may count for G-S-02; G-S-03 additionally requires explicit human confirmation of current candidate fingerprints. AI conflicts are retained as proposals and never overwrite human decisions. Substantive changes invalidate confirmation; unrelated metadata corrections do not.
+
+Use `patentkit review migrate-assessments [--apply]` to extend an existing schema without inventing human provenance or upgrading sources. Use `review export --format json --out assessment.json`, then `review assess assessment.json --actor ai --by model-name [--apply]`. After actual human review, submit an explicit JSON list of candidate_id/expected_fingerprint pairs with `review confirm confirm.json --by reviewer-name [--apply]`. All commands default to dry-run.
+
+Each assessed axis requires problem and means scores, original-text quotations, locations and rationales. JSON sources use JSON Pointer; UTF-8 text uses line ranges. Run `review assess --help` and see the companion skill references/07-assessment-protocol.md for the complete data contract. V029/V030 expose missing/stale judgments and confirmation. CLI identity is a recorded assertion, not authentication of a natural person.
