-# Patent Research, Drafting & Editing
-
-> An integrated workspace + toolchain for patent **prior-art search / novelty self-check / search evidence chain / drafting assistance**.
-> Three deliverables: the **skill package** (for AI clients), the **`patentkit` core** (pip package), and the **workspace data** (private, local).
-
-**Current versions**: skill package [`skill-v2.3.0`](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/skill-v2.3.0) ·
-core [`patentkit-v0.1.1`](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/patentkit-v0.1.1)
-(see [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) for changes)
-
-## Quick start (pick the row for your role)
-
-| I want to… | Start here |
-|---|---|
-| **Use the skill for patent research / self-checks** (Claude Code / Codex CLI / Codex desktop) | Download the [skill package release](https://github.com/cyy1018abc-kyy/Patent-Research-and-Drafting-and-Editing-/releases/tag/skill-v2.3.0) → install per [`patent-research-skill/README.md`](patent-research-skill/README.md) |
-| **Develop / extend the core** | `pip install -e ".[mcp,dev]"` → `python -m pytest` → [`patentkit/`](patentkit/) |
-| **Work in this workspace** (search / comparison / gates / delivery) | `cd` to the repo root (where `workspace.yml` lives) → follow [`docs/operations_manual.md`](docs/operations_manual.md) |
-| **Do client adaptation / cut releases** | [`release/README.md`](release/README.md), [`cross_client_tests/README.md`](cross_client_tests/README.md) |
-
-> The workspace is located by **walking up from the current directory** to find `workspace.yml`; run it elsewhere and it reports "workspace not found".
-> To use it from any directory: `$env:PATENTKIT_WORKSPACE = "<repo-root>"` (or specify `--root` for a single run).
-
-## Repository layout
-
-```
-├── README.md                 This file: entry point / quick start / layout
-├── CHANGELOG.md              Version changes for both release artifacts (skill package / core)
-├── workspace.yml             ★ Workspace marker (read by `patentkit` to locate the workspace)
-├── INDEX.md                  Workspace content index (generated by patentkit index --write)
-├── pyproject.toml            ★ pip package definition (patentkit)
-├── patentkit/                ★ Core: validation / gates / ingest / reports / MCP adapter
-├── patent-research-skill/    ★ Independently distributed skill package (SKILL.md + references + scripts + assets)
-├── release/                  Release sources (install scripts + release notes under notes/) and release process
-├── tools/                    Build / snapshot / release helper scripts
-├── tests/                    Rule regression tests (pytest; all green is the bar)
-├── docs/                     ★ Project documentation
-│   ├── operations_manual.md           From zero to delivery (commands + checkpoints + troubleshooting)
-│   ├── roadmap.md             Current roadmap: Skill-first P0–P4 (MCP frozen)
-│   ├── delivery_summary.md           Evidence-chain snapshot (generated by tools/snapshot.py)
-│   ├── release_gates_todo.md      Release gate tracking (✅ closed)
-│   ├── upgrade_plan.md         Historical baseline: 2026-10-15 diagnosis and implementation record
-│   ├── plugin_plan.md         Client-adaptation architecture analysis (roadmap section superseded)
-│   ├── public_repo_assessment.md       Risks, options, and checklist for going public (read this first)
-│   └── tool_benchmarks/             Research notes including security scanning (SkillSpector)
-├── cross_client_tests/             P3 test assets (cases/runner/validator/evidence)
-├── 00_methodology/ ~ 08_polishing/     Workspace data (search plan/logs/candidates/comparison/conclusions/drafting/polishing)
-└── .github/                  CI (install this package + full pytest + validate)
-```
-
-> `00–08` is **workspace data** (includes derived content from unpublished applications), kept separate from the code / skill package;
-> the backend data boundary is described under "Confidentiality boundary review" below.
